---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Base title="Zagros — Shared security knowledge for your team’s AI agents" description="Zagros is a self-hosted security knowledge service that gives teams and AI agents one shared reference built from authoritative CVE, CWE, ASVS, CAPEC and ATT&CK sources with preserved provenance.">
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="hero">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <div class="status"><span class="dot"></span>v0.1.0 · rust · helixdb · mcp · bm25</div>
        <h1>Trusted security knowledge for your team’s AI agents.</h1>
        <p class="lede">Run Zagros on infrastructure your team controls and give developers, AI agents, IDE integrations, and internal tools one shared security reference. Zagros retrieves authoritative CVE, CWE, ASVS, CAPEC, and ATT&amp;CK evidence with preserved provenance through MCP, CLI, and the web UI.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="hero-art">
        <img src={`${base}zagros.png`} alt="Zagros — octopus over mountains, MCP shield" width="340" height="340" />
      </figure>
      <div class="cta-row hero-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={`${base}install/`}>Install Zagros</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={`${base}install-prompt/`}>AI install</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={`${base}demo/`}>Browser preview</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://codespaces.new/siamakhaz/Zagros?quickstart=1">Try live ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="terminal">
      <div class="term-bar"><span>$ zagros search "remote code execution" --top-k 5</span><span class="spacer"></span><button class="copy-lite" data-copy='zagros search "remote code execution" --top-k 5'>copy</button></div>
      <div class="term-body">
        <div><span class="o">CVE-2024-3094</span></div>
        <div><span class="c">XZ Utils supply-chain compromise affecting upstream xz/liblzma release artifacts.</span></div>
        <div><span class="d">src</span> <a href="https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2024-3094">cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2024-3094</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="terminal">
      <div class="term-bar"><span>$ zagros know "out-of-bounds write" --top-k 5</span><span class="spacer"></span><button class="copy-lite" data-copy='zagros know "out-of-bounds write" --top-k 5'>copy</button></div>
      <div class="term-body">
        <div><span class="o">CWE-787 [CWE]</span></div>
        <div><span class="c">Out-of-bounds Write — writes past the end of the intended buffer.</span></div>
        <div><span class="d">src</span> <a href="https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html">cwe.mitre.org/definitions/787</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="sub" style="margin-top:12px">Command examples above show the interface, not captured runtime ranking or scores. Zagros keeps CVE and security-knowledge retrieval separate and currently uses lexical BM25 retrieval only — no embeddings and no generated answers. The value is a consistent evidence source that many team tools and agents can share.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="kicker">Shared reference</div>
    <h2>One team-controlled service. Five authoritative sources.</h2>
    <p class="sub">A fresh database is empty until seeded. Counts below are a 2026-09-08 seeding snapshot (~3,100 nodes) — a dated baseline, not guaranteed live counts. Verify any instance with <span class="mono">status</span>.</p>
    <div class="card feature"><div class="num">~500</div><div><span class="tag">cvelistV5 deltaLog · snapshot</span><h3>CVE records</h3><p>Exact-ID lookup plus BM25 ranked search with source URLs on every hit.</p></div></div>
    <div class="grid2">
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">MITRE CWE · snapshot</span><div class="num">969</div><h3>Weaknesses</h3><p>Know <span class="mono">CWE-787</span>? Zagros does.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">OWASP ASVS · snapshot</span><div class="num">345</div><h3>Requirements</h3><p>Search verifiable application-security requirements.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">MITRE CAPEC · snapshot</span><div class="num">613</div><h3>Attack patterns</h3><p>Search documented attack patterns.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">MITRE ATT&amp;CK · snapshot</span><div class="num">697</div><h3>Techniques</h3><p>Enterprise ATT&amp;CK techniques, queryable locally.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="kicker">Install</div>
    <h2>Up in three steps.</h2>
    <p class="sub">Prereqs: Git, Docker + Compose v2. No local Rust toolchain needed — commands run in the Compose <span class="mono">cli</span> profile container. Full walkthrough: <a href={`${base}install/`}>Install →</a></p>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step"><div class="n">1</div><div><h3>Start the stack <button class="copy-lite" data-copy="docker compose -f docker/compose.yml up -d --build">copy</button></h3><p>HelixDB on <span class="mono">127.0.0.1:47474</span>, MCP on <span class="mono">127.0.0.1:8789</span>, UI on <span class="mono">127.0.0.1:8788</span>.</p><pre class="code">docker compose -f docker/compose.yml up -d --build</pre></div></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="n">2</div><div><h3>Seed the index <button class="copy-lite" data-copy="docker compose -f docker/compose.yml --profile cli run --rm cli backfill --limit 500">copy</button></h3><p>Idempotent — safe to re-run. Then load knowledge sources with <span class="mono">source all</span> in the same container.</p><pre class="code"><span class="cm"># CVE baseline, then knowledge sources</span>
docker compose -f docker/compose.yml --profile cli run --rm cli backfill --limit 500
docker compose -f docker/compose.yml --profile cli run --rm cli source all</pre></div></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="n">3</div><div><h3>Connect your team’s agents</h3><p>Use one protected Streamable HTTP MCP endpoint from compatible harnesses and internal tools. The default local endpoint is shown below; for a shared deployment, expose Zagros through your authenticated internal gateway or reverse proxy.</p><pre class="code"># local default
http://localhost:8789/mcp

# shared deployment example
https://zagros.example.com/mcp</pre></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="cta-row" style="justify-content:flex-start">
      <a class="btn btn-primary mono" href={`${base}install/`}>Install Zagros →</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost mono" href={`${base}install-prompt/`}>AI install →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="kicker">AI integration</div>
    <h2>One shared reference for many agents.</h2>
    <p class="sub">Zagros exposes the same seven tools over stdio (<span class="mono">zagros-mcp</span>) and Streamable HTTP (<span class="mono">zagros-mcp-http</span>), so multiple agents and internal tools can query the same controlled corpus. MCP results include source URLs and provenance; Zagros retrieves evidence and leaves analysis and recommendations to the consuming agent.</p>
    <div class="grid2">
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">search_cves</span><h3>Ranked CVE search</h3><p>BM25 + field weights, exact-match &amp; phrase bonuses.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">get_cve</span><h3>Exact CVE lookup</h3><p><span class="mono">CVE-2024-3094</span> → full record + source URL.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">index_status</span><h3>Index health</h3><p>Counts, refresh state, and per-source integrity/freshness health.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">sync_cves</span><h3>Delta sync</h3><p>Pull latest CVE changes. Approval-required, 5-min cooldown.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">search_knowledge</span><h3>Knowledge search</h3><p>Ranked CWE / ASVS / CAPEC / ATT&amp;CK retrieval.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">sync_knowledge_source</span><h3>Knowledge sync</h3><p>Refresh one knowledge source or all. Approval-required.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">backfill_cves</span><h3>CVE history backfill</h3><p>Walk deltaLog history with explicit approval and rate limiting.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="cta-row" style="justify-content:flex-start">
      <a class="btn btn-ghost mono" href={`${base}demo/`}>Browser preview →</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost mono" href={`${base}docs/mcp/`}>MCP reference →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
</Base>